            "title": "ABOUT NANGA: A Passion for Taking on Challenges"
          }
        },
        "about_story_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>\"NANGA\" takes its name from Nanga Parbat, an 8,126-meter peak in the Himalayas known and feared as the \"Man-Eater Mountain.\" NANGA was founded in 1994 in Maibara, Shiga Prefecture, as a down product manufacturer. Named after a formidable peak that has claimed the lives of many climbers, the brand embodies the spirit of taking on difficult challenges. It carries the conviction of second-generation president Akira Yokota, who believed that difficulty is exactly the reason to take something on, and that NANGA should climb where others have not.</p><p>In this region, long known for Omi silk floss futons, NANGA inherited the techniques and expertise of a futon manufacturer that supported the local industry for over 50 years, and has grown for 30 years since. This pride as a factory brand carries through into outdoor gear and apparel built for demanding conditions, and our down products are now making their way out into the world.</p>"
          }
        }
